    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0246" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660F.116/163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Praha</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-08T12:00:00+01:00">April 8,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 8—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. My No. 11, March 4, 11 a.m. Collection of laws and decrees of April 1st
                    contains regulation of National Bank concerning certain changes in the
                    Czechoslovak-German Clearing Arrangement provide for reichsmark payments on
                    transit goods through Germany at the following rates: cotton 2½%; other
                    merchandise 1 to 4%. Please see Commercial Attaché’s special reports numbers
                    140, 142 and 147.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d138-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
